'''
new_txt_from_audio_[GUI.py]

Portable Tkinter GUI for reading a transcript while listening to the
matching audio file.

Purpose
-------
Open an audio file and a matching transcript, play the audio, and keep
the text synchronized with playback:

* the line currently being heard is highlighted and scrolled into view
  as the audio plays (auto-sync)
* Ctrl+click or double-click any line seeks the audio to that line's
  timestamp, computed from the exact parsed time (not a rough estimate)
* search highlights every match and jumps between matches; jumping also
  seeks the audio to the matched line
* the transcript can be saved as plain text or exported as LRC

Supported file types (the same set the console script supports)
---------------------------------------------------------------
Audio: WAV, MP3, FLAC, OGG, OPUS, M4A/AAC, WMA
Text:  TXT, LRC ([mm:ss.ms]), SRT, JSON segments, plain MD/TXT

Audio playback uses pygame (optional). When it is not installed the app
still opens, parses and searches transcripts; it offers to install
pygame into the ./libs folder beside this script so the whole folder
stays portable (nothing is ever installed into the operating system).

Optional: tkinterdnd2 enables dropping audio/text files onto the window.

Layout beside this script:
  libs/               optional pip packages (pygame, tkinterdnd2)
'''

